From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:10:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Describe codes where they are read and judged, not only where
 typed

Descriptions reached only the coder and auditor forms and the key
editors. They now also appear on the post-submit review and its Excel
export, the trainer's scoring notes, DRG Review, the CC/MCC key check,
the trainer's auditor review, and as hover titles on most-missed codes.

Every description wraps or truncates inside its own column, verified on
each screen with the longest real titles: no row or page overflows. A
code matching on both sides is described once, not twice.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
